{"senses": [{"examples": [{"text": "He was surrounded, so gave himself up.", "bold_text_offsets": [[22, 26], [35, 37]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "They gave him up to the police.", "bold_text_offsets": [[5, 9], [14, 16]], "type": "example"}], "categories": ["English terms with usage examples", "English transitive verbs"], "links": [["surrender", "surrender"], ["inform", "inform"]], "synonyms": [{"word": "surrender"}, {"word": "yield"}], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive) To surrender (someone or something); to inform on (someone)."], "glosses": ["To surrender (someone or something); to inform on (someone)."], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "He gave up his seat to an old man.", "bold_text_offsets": [[3, 10]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "The king gave up land in exchange for peace.", "bold_text_offsets": [[9, 16]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "\"Dear Miss Woodhouse, I would not give up the pleasure and honour of being intimate with you for any thing in the world.\"", "ref": "1816, Jane Austen, chapter 7, in Emma, volume 1:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[34, 41]]}], "categories": ["English terms with quotations", "English terms with usage examples", "English transitive verbs", "Quotation templates to be cleaned"], "links": [["relinquish", "relinquish"]], "synonyms": [{"word": "forlend", "tags": ["archaic"]}, {"word": "surrender"}, {"word": "yield"}], "coordinate_terms": [{"word": "give away"}], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive) To relinquish (something)"], "glosses": ["To relinquish (something)"], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "I gave myself up to working for this cause.", "bold_text_offsets": [[2, 6], [14, 16]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "She persuaded us to give up our time to the project.", "bold_text_offsets": [[20, 27]], "type": "example"}], "categories": ["English terms with usage examples", "English transitive verbs"], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive) Devote or dedicate (oneself, one's life, etc.) to something."], "glosses": ["Devote or dedicate (oneself, one's life, etc.) to something."], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "A good pitcher will give up very few home runs.", "bold_text_offsets": [[20, 27]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Don't tell them where you are, and try not to give up any clues either.", "bold_text_offsets": [[46, 53]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Fiers, who now pitches for the Oakland Athletics, has gone 27-12 with a no-hitter in two years since leaving the Astros. But the last time he faced them, on Sept. 9, he gave up nine runs, including five homers, and got just three outs.", "ref": "2019 November 14, Tyler Kepner, “After Reports of Astros' Cheating, M.L.B. Is Left to Restore Trust”, in The New York Times, New York, N.Y.: The New York Times Company, →ISSN, →OCLC, archived from the original on 15 Jan 2023:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[169, 176]]}], "categories": ["English terms with quotations", "English terms with usage examples", "English transitive verbs"], "links": [["concede", "concede"]], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive) To have someone obtain (something) to one's disadvantage; to concede."], "glosses": ["To have someone obtain (something) to one's disadvantage; to concede."], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "They gave up the search when it got dark.", "bold_text_offsets": [[5, 12]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Once again, the WiFi isn't willing to work. When the guard comes to check tickets, I ask him if it ever works. He rolls his eyes and tells me it rarely does. He says I'll be lucky if I get it to connect. I give up trying.", "ref": "2025 October 15, 'Mystery Shopper', “About Anglia... and high scores”, in RAIL, number 1046, page 54:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[206, 213]]}, {"text": "A year after Tristan’s funeral, his grandma visited his grave, but she saw it had been dug up to 1.2 meters. Whoever had done it hadn’t managed to reach the boy’s coffin, and it looked like they had given up midway.", "ref": "2026 September 6, Aniket Chaughule, “Tristan Brübach, 13, Was Murdered in 1998. His Killer May Have Called Police and Later Returned to His Grave”, in Skip Boring, archived from the original on 08 Sep 2026:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[199, 207]]}], "categories": ["English terms with quotations", "English terms with usage examples", "English transitive verbs"], "links": [["stop", "stop"], ["quit", "quit"]], "synonyms": [{"word": "cease"}, {"word": "discontinue"}, {"word": "blin"}, {"word": "turn away from", "alt": "sth undesirable"}], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive) To stop or quit (an activity, etc.)."], "glosses": ["To stop or quit (an activity, etc.)."], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "I gave up my faith years ago.", "bold_text_offsets": [[2, 9]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "The semi-streamlined contour of the earlier G.W.R. railcars has been given up in favour of a more utilitarian blunt-nose end, and effective floor space gained thereby.", "ref": "1941 October, “Notes and News: Great Western Parcels Railcar”, in Railway Magazine, page 474:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[69, 77]]}, {"text": "Never gonna give you up / Never gonna let you down / Never gonna run around and desert you", "ref": "1987, Stock Aitken Waterman, “Never Gonna Give You Up”, in Whenever You Need Somebody, performed by Rick Astley:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[12, 23]]}, {"text": "The optimistic peace-and-love philosophy of his youth having given him up, he no longer knew how to reconcile himself to an increasingly phoney (he loathed, in this context, the otherwise excellent word “virtual”) reality.", "ref": "2001, Salman Rushdie, Fury: A Novel, London: Jonathan Cape, →ISBN, page 7:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[61, 66], [71, 73]]}, {"text": "\"I tried retirement ten years ago. Didn't think much of it. Complete waste of time. So I gave it up after two weeks.\"", "ref": "2021 November 3, Adrian Shooter talks to Paul Clifton, “A lifetime of railway achievements”, in RAIL, number 943, page 34:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[89, 99]]}], "categories": ["English terms with quotations", "English terms with usage examples", "English transitive verbs"], "links": [["abandon", "abandon"]], "synonyms": [{"word": "desert"}, {"word": "forlet", "tags": ["dialectal", "obsolete"]}, {"word": "forsake"}], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive) To abandon (someone or something)"], "glosses": ["To abandon (someone or something)"], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "They gave him up for dead.", "bold_text_offsets": [[5, 16]], "type": "example"}], "categories": ["English terms with usage examples", "English transitive verbs"], "links": [["lose", "lose"], ["hope", "hope"]], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive) To lose hope concerning (someone or something)"], "glosses": ["To lose hope concerning (someone or something)"], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "OK, I give up, you win.", "bold_text_offsets": [[6, 13]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Wake in a sweat again / Another day's been laid to waste / In my disgrace / Stuck in my head again / Feels like I'll never leave this place / There's no escape / I'm my own worst enemy / I've given up / I'm sick of feeling / Is there nothing you can say? / Take this all away / I'm suffocating", "ref": "2007, “Given Up”, Mike Shinoda (lyrics), performed by Linkin Park:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[192, 200]]}], "categories": ["English intransitive verbs", "English terms with quotations", "English terms with usage examples"], "links": [["admit", "admit"], ["defeat", "defeat"], ["capitulate", "capitulate"], ["desist", "desist"]], "synonyms": [{"word": "capitulate"}, {"word": "give in"}, {"word": "surrender"}, {"word": "throw in the towel"}, {"word": "wave the white flag"}], "coordinate_terms": [{"word": "give out"}, {"word": "give way"}], "raw_glosses": ["(intransitive) To admit defeat, capitulate; to desist for that reason."], "glosses": ["To admit defeat, capitulate; to desist for that reason."], "tags": ["intransitive"]}, {"topics": ["business", "finance"], "categories": ["English transitive verbs", "en:Finance"], "links": [["finance", "finance#Noun"], ["execute", "execute"], ["trade", "trade"], ["on behalf of", "on behalf of"], ["broker", "broker"]], "raw_glosses": ["(transitive, finance) To execute a trade on behalf of another broker."], "glosses": ["To execute a trade on behalf of another broker."], "tags": ["transitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "The next morning, Sunday, I was boxing with R., who had come over with three or four others to swap a few with me. I was given up to be the best boxer around, and I laid them cold as fast as they came at me.", "ref": "1969, God Struck Me Dead; Religious Conversion Experiences and Autobiographies of Ex-Slaves, Philadelphia, P.A.; Boston, M.A.: Pilgrim Press, page 45:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[121, 129]]}], "categories": ["American English", "English dialectal terms", "English intransitive verbs", "English terms with quotations"], "links": [["acknowledge", "acknowledge#Verb"], ["recognize", "recognize#Verb"]], "raw_glosses": ["(intransitive, US dialectal) To acknowledge, recognize as."], "glosses": ["To acknowledge, recognize as."], "tags": ["US", "dialectal", "intransitive"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "He gave up that he was the one who opened the door.", "bold_text_offsets": [[3, 10]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Well, give it up, Prof! What did you find out!", "ref": "2004, Intelligent Systems, translated by Nintendo of America, Paper Mario: The Thousand-Year Door, Nintendo, GameCube, level/area: Rogueport:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[6, 16]]}], "categories": ["American English", "English intransitive verbs", "English slang", "English terms with quotations", "English terms with usage examples"], "raw_glosses": ["(intransitive, US, slang) To reveal (something)."], 